nc0,-2,0.3,-3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1272em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 要么有理要么无理」。对布劳威尔和直觉主义者而言，这样的「存在证明」是空头支票：它断言存在却拿不出实物，因而不是合法的数学。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念\">核心概念</h2><p>直觉主义把数学看作人心的构造活动，而非对独立王国的发现——这与<a href=\"../ontology/platonism-mathematical-objects\">柏拉图主义</a>针锋相对。由此引出它最惊人的主张：对无穷领域不能无限制地使用排中律 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P \\lor \\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span>，因为「<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 为真」必须意味着「我们能构造出 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明」，而对无穷对象我们未必能在 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 之间做出构造性的判定。下图勾勒这条逻辑链及其分支。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"graph\" data-source=\"graph TD&#10;  A[布劳威尔:&lt;br/&gt;数学是心智构造] --&gt; B[存在 = 能被构造]&#10;  B --&gt; C[拒绝无限制排中律&lt;br/&gt;P 或 非P]&#10;  C --&gt; D[拒绝非构造性&lt;br/&gt;存在证明]&#10;  A --&gt; E[海廷:&lt;br/&gt;直觉主义逻辑形式化]&#10;  E --&gt; F[BHK 解释:&lt;br/&gt;证明即构造]&#10;  B --&gt; G[毕晓普:&lt;br/&gt;构造性分析]&#10;  B --&gt; H[马丁-洛夫:&lt;br/&gt;直觉类型论]&#10;  H --&gt; I[命题即类型&lt;br/&gt;证明即程序]\">graph TD\n  A[布劳威尔:&lt;br/&gt;数学是心智构造] --&gt; B[存在 = 能被构造]\n  B --&gt; C[拒绝无限制排中律&lt;br/&gt;P 或 非P]\n  C --&gt; D[拒绝非构造性&lt;br/&gt;存在证明]\n  A --&gt; E[海廷:&lt;br/&gt;直觉主义逻辑形式化]\n  E --&gt; F[BHK 解释:&lt;br/&gt;证明即构造]\n  B --&gt; G[毕晓普:&lt;br/&gt;构造性分析]\n  B --&gt; H[马丁-洛夫:&lt;br/&gt;直觉类型论]\n  H --&gt; I[命题即类型&lt;br/&gt;证明即程序]</pre><p>下表对比经典数学与直觉主义在几个核心点上的分歧：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>议题</th>\n<th>经典数学</th>\n<th>直觉主义</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>排中律 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\lor\\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span></td>\n<td>普遍有效</td>\n<td>仅当能判定时才有效</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>双重否定 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\neg\\neg P \\to P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span></td>\n<td>成立</td>\n<td>一般不成立</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>「存在 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></span>」</td>\n<td>可非构造地断言</td>\n<td>必须给出构造 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></span> 的方法</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>数学对象</td>\n<td>独立存在（实在论）</td>\n<td>心智构造的产物</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>实无穷</td>\n<td>接受</td>\n<td>只接受潜无穷</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"布劳威尔的构造性纲领\">布劳威尔的构造性纲领</h2><p>L. E. J. 布劳威尔在 1907 年的博士论文中点燃了这场革命。他的哲学根基是康德式的：数学不来自逻辑、也不来自经验，而来自人心对「时间中的二一性」的纯直观——先有 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span></span>，再有 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span></span>，无穷尽地生成自然数。数学对象因此是人构造出来的，不是某个抽象天国里现成的居民。</p>\n<p>由这个根基，排中律的失效是必然推论。说「<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 为真」对直觉主义者意味着「我们手里有 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的一个构造性证明」，说「<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 为真」意味着「我们有一个把任何 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明转化为矛盾的方法」。现在考虑某个尚未解决的猜想 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span>（比如关于某个无穷过程的断言）：我们既没有 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的构造，也没有 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的构造，那么断言「<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\lor\\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span>」就毫无根据。布劳威尔由此拒绝把对有限情形成立的排中律盲目外推到无穷——他只接受潜无穷（永远可以再加一），拒斥实无穷（一个已完成的无穷整体）。这种对实无穷的警惕，与康托尔在<a href=\"../contemporary/set-theory-and-infinity\">集合论与无穷</a>中放纵实无穷的立场恰成两极。</p>\n<p>代价是真切的：直觉主义放弃了大量经典定理（如波尔查诺—魏尔斯特拉斯定理、每个实数要么有理要么无理），数学家普遍不愿付这个价，这也是希尔伯特激烈反对布劳威尔的原因，详见<a href=\"formalism-hilbert-godel\">形式主义、希尔伯特纲领与哥德尔</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"bhk-解释与直觉主义逻辑\">BHK 解释与直觉主义逻辑</h2><p>布劳威尔本人轻视形式化，但他的学生阿伦德·海廷把直觉主义逻辑写成了精确的形式系统，使它从一种哲学态度变成可操作的演算。其语义核心是「BHK 解释」（布劳威尔—海廷—柯尔莫哥洛夫），它不按真值、而按「什么算作一个证明」来定义每个联结词：</p>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P \\land Q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∧</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明，是一个 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明加一个 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明；<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P \\lor Q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明，是「<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明」或「<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明」再加上标明是哪一个的标记（这正是排中律失效的根源——你必须指明是哪一支）；<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P \\to Q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明，是一个把任何 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明转化为 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明的方法；<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>x</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\exists x\\, P(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∃</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明，是一个具体的 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></span> 加上 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 的证明（这正是非构造存在证明被拒的根源）。</p>\n<p>BHK 解释的深远意义在于它把「证明」等同于「构造」乃至「程序」，从而在直觉主义逻辑与计算之间架起桥梁——这一桥梁在下一节展开，并直接通向当代<a href=\"../contemporary/computation-proof-ai-mathematics\">计算、证明与 AI 数学</a>中证明助手的理论基础。</p>\n<h2 id=\"毕晓普的构造分析与类型论\">毕晓普的构造分析与类型论</h2><p>直觉主义曾被诟病为「只破不立」。1967 年埃雷特·毕晓普的《构造性分析基础》改变了这一印象：他证明分析学的大部分实质内容（连续函数、微积分、测度论的可观片段）都能在严格构造性的框架内重建，且不必依赖布劳威尔那些古怪的「选择序列」假设。毕晓普表明构造性数学不是残废的经典数学，而是一门信息量更丰富的数学——每个存在定理都自带一个算法。</p>\n<p>更深远的发展是佩尔·马丁-洛夫的「直觉类型论」（1970 年代）。它把 BHK 解释推到极致，确立「命题即类型、证明即程序」的对应（库里—霍华德对应的强化）：证明一个定理，字面上就是写出一个具有相应类型的程序。这使数学证明与可执行代码合二为一，成为今天 Coq、Agda、Lean 等证明助手的理论基石。这条「证明即程序」的线索，把布劳威尔一百年前关于「存在即构造」的哲学坚持，意外地变成了 21 世纪机器形式化数学的工程现实，详见<a href=\"../contemporary/computation-proof-ai-mathematics\">计算、证明与 AI 数学</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"构造性与经典数学的代价清单\">构造性与经典数学的代价清单</h2><p>拒绝排中律不是无损的偏好选择，它系统地改写了哪些经典定理还能成立：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>经典定理 / 工具</th>\n<th>在直觉主义下的命运</th>\n<th>原因</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>排中律 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\lor\\neg P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span></td>\n<td>仅当可判定时才有效</td>\n<td>无穷对象未必能构造地判定</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>双重否定消去 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\neg\\neg P\\to P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span></td>\n<td>一般不成立</td>\n<td>无构造即不可推出 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>「每个实数要么有理要么无理」</td>\n<td>不成立</td>\n<td>判定依赖非构造的排中</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>波尔查诺—魏尔斯特拉斯定理</td>\n<td>不成立</td>\n<td>依赖实无穷与排中</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>非构造存在证明</td>\n<td>无效</td>\n<td>断言存在却拿不出构造物</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>直觉主义视数学为心智的构造活动，「存在」必须意味着「能被构造」，由此拒绝对无穷领域无限制使用排中律和非构造性存在证明。</li>\n<li>它与<a href=\"../ontology/platonism-mathematical-objects\">柏拉图主义</a>的实在论、与康托尔式实无穷（见<a href=\"../contemporary/set-theory-and-infinity\">集合论与无穷</a>）都正面冲突。</li>\n<li>海廷的形式化与 BHK 解释把它变成精确演算，核心是「按构造而非真值定义联结词」。</li>\n<li>毕晓普证明分析可构造性重建（存在定理自带算法），马丁-洛夫的类型论确立「命题即类型、证明即程序」。</li>\n<li>这条「证明即构造即程序」的脉络，成了当代<a href=\"../contemporary/computation-proof-ai-mathematics\">计算、证明与 AI 数学</a>中证明助手的哲学与技术源头，也使直觉主义成为今天最具实践生命力的基础学派。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"直觉主义与构造主义","id":"直觉主义与构造主义"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"布劳威尔的构造性纲领","id":"布劳威尔的构造性纲领"},{"level":2,"text":"BHK 解释与直觉主义逻辑","id":"bhk-解释与直觉主义逻辑"},{"level":2,"text":"毕晓普的构造分析与类型论","id":"毕晓普的构造分析与类型论"},{"level":2,"text":"构造性与经典数学的代价清单","id":"构造性与经典数学的代价清单"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"逻辑主义（弗雷格与罗素）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-mathematics/foundational-schools/logicism-frege-russell"},"next":{"title":"形式主义、希尔伯特纲领与哥德尔","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-mathematics/foundational-schools/formalism-hilbert-godel"}}